---
import ArrowIcon from "../components/ArrowIcon.astro";
import ToolDirectory from "../components/ToolDirectory.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Prepare SEO and Developer Data Locally"
  description="Turn keyword exports, URL sets, indexability evidence, and MCP messages into reviewable files without uploading the input."
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <section class="workbench-hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
    <div class="workbench-hero-copy">
      <h1 id="home-title">Turn raw SEO exports into inputs you can review and reuse.</h1>
      <p>Load a local export, map its columns, review conflicts or exclusions, and hand off a checked result. Everything runs in your browser.</p>
      <div class="toolbox-actions">
        <a class="toolbox-button" href="/workflows/prepare-keyword-import">Prepare a keyword import <ArrowIcon /></a>
        <a class="workbench-text-link" href="/workflows/build-clean-crawl-list">Build a crawl list <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-flagship-preview" aria-label="Flagship workflow preview">
      <a href="/workflows/prepare-keyword-import">
        <span class="hero-flagship-number">01</span>
        <div><strong>Prepare a keyword import</strong><p>Map columns → find conflicting duplicates → choose a resolution → export the reviewed file</p></div>
        <ArrowIcon />
      </a>
      <a href="/workflows/build-clean-crawl-list">
        <span class="hero-flagship-number">02</span>
        <div><strong>Build a clean crawl list</strong><p>Extract URLs → define scope → inspect exclusions → export targets and rejection reasons</p></div>
        <ArrowIcon />
      </a>
      <div class="hero-recipe-note"><strong>Portable recipes + run manifests</strong><span>Reuse the rules, then bind one input and output with private SHA-256 receipts.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="flagship-workflows" aria-labelledby="flagship-title">
    <div class="flagship-intro">
      <span>Start with a real job</span>
      <h2 id="flagship-title">Two workbenches that leave you with a checked file.</h2>
      <p>Each workflow keeps the source local, shows the rows that need a decision, and exports both the usable result and the evidence behind it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flagship-workflow-grid">
      <article>
        <div class="flagship-card-head"><span>Keyword import</span><strong>CSV · TSV · TXT</strong></div>
        <h3>Clean the file without hiding conflicting metrics.</h3>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Map</strong><span>Find keyword, volume, intent, language, and the columns you need to retain.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Review</strong><span>See duplicate keywords whose extra columns disagree. Choose first, last, merge, or manual review.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Export</strong><span>Download the reviewed table, a reusable recipe, and an optional run manifest.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <a href="/workflows/prepare-keyword-import">Prepare a keyword import <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="flagship-card-head"><span>Crawl input</span><strong>XML · CSV · TSV · TXT</strong></div>
        <h3>Build a crawl plan, not just a shorter URL list.</h3>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Scope</strong><span>Choose host, subdomains, protocol, include rules, exclusions, and resource handling.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Review</strong><span>Separate crawlable pages, robots blocks, resources, invalid URLs, and manual checks.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Export</strong><span>Download crawl targets and rejected URLs with the exact reason for each decision.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <a href="/workflows/build-clean-crawl-list">Build a clean crawl list <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-workflow-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <div class="section-heading-row"><div><h2 id="workflow-title">Two more jobs, when the input is evidence or a protocol message.</h2><p>The first two workbenches prepare data. These two help explain a technical result.</p></div><a href="/workflows">All workflows <ArrowIcon /></a></div>
    <div class="secondary-workflows">
      <a href="/workflows/debug-indexability"><strong>Debug indexability</strong><span>Paste headers, rendered head markup, and robots.txt. Extract the signals before reading the verdict.</span><ArrowIcon /></a>
      <a href="/workflows/validate-mcp-message"><strong>Validate an MCP message</strong><span>Choose the protocol revision, import a log, correct the structure, and compare expected with actual JSON.</span><ArrowIcon /></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="quick-tool-section" aria-labelledby="quick-tools-title">
    <div class="section-heading-row">
      <div>
        <h2 id="quick-tools-title">Quick tools for the small stuff.</h2>
        <p>Open one focused utility when you already know the exact transformation you need.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/tools">All tools <ArrowIcon /></a>
    </div>
    <ToolDirectory />
  </section>

  <section class="change-example" aria-labelledby="change-example-title">
    <div class="change-example-heading">
      <h2 id="change-example-title">A result is useful when you know what changed.</h2>
      <p>The URL workflow shows the cleaned list and the decisions that produced it. Nothing is crawled in the background.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="change-example-panes">
      <div>
        <span>Before</span>
        <pre>https://EXAMPLE.com/
https://example.com
https://example.com/page/#top
https://example.com/page?utm_source=news
https://example.com/about/</pre>
      </div>
      <ArrowIcon />
      <div class="change-example-after">
        <span>After · 3 unique URLs</span>
        <pre>https://example.com/
https://example.com/page
https://example.com/about</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="change-summary">Duplicate root removed. Host normalized. Fragment, tracking parameter, and trailing path slashes removed.</p>
    <a class="workbench-text-link" href="/workflows/build-clean-crawl-list">See the crawl-list workflow <ArrowIcon /></a>
  </section>

  <section class="private-band" aria-labelledby="private-title">
    <div class="private-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
    <div>
      <h2 id="private-title">Private by default.</h2>
      <p>No account, no uploads, and no saved input. Anonymous usage events never include tool inputs or generated outputs.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="evidence-entry" aria-labelledby="evidence-entry-title">
    <div>
      <h2 id="evidence-entry-title">Examples, limits, and evidence.</h2>
      <p>The useful details live next to the job: realistic inputs, edge cases, technical limits, and reproducible tests.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-links">
      <a href="/guides"><strong>Practical guides</strong><span>Use a method when the decision matters more than the transformation.</span><ArrowIcon /></a>
      <a href="/workflows"><strong>Tested edge cases</strong><span>See how the main workflows handle messy inputs and ambiguous signals.</span><ArrowIcon /></a>
      <a href="/field-tests"><strong>Published field tests</strong><span>Inspect the repository fixtures, runners, results, and review limits.</span><ArrowIcon /></a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
